    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The Los Vegas Valley Shear Zone is a poorly-exposed, major right-lateral fault in the Basin and Range. Along the Las Vegas Valley, three distinct basins are identified from regional gravity data.The basins are aligned in a right-stepping pattern. Utilizing the assumption that the interactions of discontinuous fault segments generate deformation consistent with the known kinematics of strike-slip faulting, it is interpreted here that the LasVegasValley Shear Zone is composed of discontinuous, right-stepping fault strands with the basins located within the right-stepovers.",
